The music streaming service Tidal said Tuesday that it would ban tracks it believes are completely AI-generated starting next month, a move its leader believes &#x201C;will resonate with both artists and listeners alike.&#x201D;

The service will remove the AI tracks starting Dec. 9, making Tidal the first music streaming platform to ban AI music entirely. It comes nearly five months after Tidal said it would demonetize any AI-powered song, force those artists to label their tracks as either AI-generated or AI-assisted and ban AI songs that were associated with &#x201C;fraudulent activity,&#x201D; a category that includes songs impersonating established artists and efforts to &#x201C;deceive listeners.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Taylor Swift's 'Law & Order: SVU' Crime Scene Evidence Board from the Emmys Goes on Display at the Paley Center (EXCLUSIVE) Taylor Swift to Perform at CMAs for the First Time in 13 Years

&#x201C;But that&#x2019;s enough, as 43% of tracks distributed to us in the last 90 days have been detected as AI-generated. Something more drastic needs to be done,&#x201D;&#xA0;wrote Robert Anderson, the Tidal Lead at parent company Block, in an X thread on Tuesday. &#x201C;We&#x2019;ll begin removing all wholly AI-generated tracks from our catalog, and you&#x2019;ll see them completely gone by the beginning of the year.&#x201D;

Anderson said that 96% of all AI-generated songs receive zero plays. The move will cleave the platform of 29 million tracks, Anderson added, and have it reject between 80,000 to 85,000 songs a day.

&#x201C;We encourage our peers to follow suit,&#x201D;&#xA0;he wrote.

The move comes as competitors such as Spotify and Apple Music continue to test approaches to combat the rise of AI-generated tracks proliferating on their platforms, many of which the services have labeled some version of &#x201C;slop&#x201D; or &#x201C;spam.&#x201D; Apple Music said it would also begin labeling AI-generated or AI-assisted tracks on its platform, while Spotify said it would label artists it deemed AI creations as an &#x201C;AI Persona.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Spotify said in a blog post last month it also removed 50 million slop or spam tracks from users' recommendations this year, which came after it removed 75 million of those songs from its catalog entirely. The revelation came among a number of updates regarding Spotify's efforts to combat AI spam.

&#x201C;This work isn&#x2019;t finished,&#x201D; Spotify added. &#x201C;AI moves fast, and bad actors adapt just as fast. But as AI makes music more abundant, we believe listeners will value human artistry even more. Our job is to make Spotify the place they find it.&#x201D;

Earlier this summer, Ed Simpson teamed with Content Partners to buy Y ouTube true-crime channel Dr. Insanity.

Wonderloom Media , founded by Wheelhouse&#x2019;s former chief strategy officer and the investment firm, is now launching a Dr. Insanity podcast.

They have teamed with Audioboom on the project. Audioboom is behind podcasts including Pod Save America and The Tim Dillon Show and distributes a number of true-crime shows such as True Crime with Kendall Rae and True Crime Obsessed with Patrick Hinds and Gillian Pensavalle. Related Stories News Ed Simpson Launches Wonderloom Media With Content Partners, Buys YouTube True-Crime Channel Dr. Insanity News Elev8on & French Wealth Manager Anato To Find European Investments For U.S. Stars

The podcast will feature in-depth, documentary-style episodes exploring real-life crime cases. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

The channel, which was founded by Jared West, has over 6M subscribers on YouTube, where it offers videos such as How Police Captured Colorado&#x2019;s Smartest Killer and When Dumb Karens Try To Attack Cops.

&#x201C;Dr. Insanity is becoming the home of true crime, and that means meeting fans wherever they listen and watch,&#x201D; said Ed Simpson, CEO of Wonderloom Media. &#x201C;Our audience has always gone deep with us, and so many of them already live with true crime in their ears. Audioboom shares our commitment to great storytelling, and we&#x2019;re excited to bring Dr. Insanity to a whole new community of listeners together.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Dr. Insanity has built an incredible audience on YouTube by delivering compelling, high-quality true crime storytelling,&#x201D; said Brendan Regan, Chief Content Officer at Audioboom. &#x201C;We see a tremendous opportunity to bring that same experience to podcast listeners and introduce the brand to new audiences. We're excited to partner with the Wonderloom team to expand Dr. Insanity's reach and build on its success across platforms.&#x201D;

&#x201C; Adult Supervision ,&#x201D; Sweden&#x2019;s entry for best international feature film at the Academy Awards, has closed further distribution deals.

The latest round of international sales, handled by Heretic , include Filmin for Spain, Lighthouse Entertainment for Germany, Pictureworks for India, Nachson Films for Israel and Xenix for Switzerland. Discussions for France are at an advanced stage.

The darkly comic feature, written and directed by Sweden&#x2019;s Alex Schulman , recently picked up two awards at the Seville European Film Festival, taking home the Puerta Am&#xE9;rica Award and the best actor award, shared by its three leads, Gustaf Skarsg&#xE5;rd (&#x201C;Vikings,&#x201D; &#x201C;Westworld&#x201D;), Fares Fares (&#x201C;The Nile Hilton Incident,&#x201D; &#x201C;Eagles of the Republic&#x201D;) and Linus Wahlgren (&#x201C;Partisan&#x201D;). It made its world premiere at Fantastic Fest in Austin, where it competed in the Next Wave Competition and won the best picture award. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Heretic previously sold the film to Fandango for Italy, Palace Films for Australia and New Zealand, Vertigo Releasing for Hungary, CinemArt for the Czech Republic and Slovakia, MCF for ex-Yugoslavia and Bulgaria, Mayfly for Poland, Inoekino for the CIS, Taip Toliau for Lithuania, Estinfilm for Estonia and Riga FF for Latvia. Broadcast rights were acquired by HBO in multiple Central and Eastern European territories after the theatrical run.

&#x201C;Adult Supervision&#x201D; follows three fathers who accompany their teenage daughters on a school trip to a remote island. What begins as a seemingly straightforward weekend away soon takes an unexpected turn, as tensions rise, old resentments surface and the boundaries between authority and violence begin to blur. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Ioanna Stais, head of sales at Heretic, said, &#x201C;It&#x2019;s incredibly rewarding to see &#x2018;Adult Supervision&#x2019; continuing to find its audience and connecting with distributors across so many different markets. We&#x2019;re particularly proud of the recognition the film has received in Seville and the journey it has had so far. We&#x2019;re excited to see that momentum continue as the film reaches new audiences internationally.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Adult Supervision&#x201D; is produced by Warner Bros. International Television Production, with Christina Legkova as producer and Johan Hedman and Sofie Palage as executive producers. It is co-produced by RMV Film, Tiisch Film, Film Stockholm and Scanbox Entertainment, with support from the Swedish Film Institute and the Swedish Agency for Economic and Regional Growth. The film is distributed in Scandinavia by Scanbox Entertainment.

Christina Legkova, producer at Warner Bros. International Television Production, said, &#x201C;Coming away from Seville with two awards is a fantastic recognition for the film. We&#x2019;re delighted to see both the film and the performances of Gustaf, Fares and Linus celebrated, and to have this moment come as &#x2018;Adult Supervision&#x2019; continues its journey as Sweden&#x2019;s Academy Awards entry makes it all the more special.&#x201D;

The film will be presented at Ventana Sur in December, as it continues its international festival and market journey.

