It took Michelle Randolph a full season to realize she was the comic relief.

At first, she played the part of Ainsley Norris &#x2014; the overly indulged, wildly inappropriate teenage daughter of Billy Bob Thornton&#x2019;s oil-industry fixer in Taylor Sheridan&#x2019;s Texas saga Landman &#x2014; as if she was a character in a Strindberg play.

She dug deep. She internalized her struggle. She committed to her choices.

Naturally, viewers thought she was hilarious. Related Stories Movies Glen Powell Is a Has-Been Country Singer in Judd Apatow's 'Comeback King' Trailer Movies Brandon Sklenar on 'Iron Jane,' Body Dysmorphia and His Rapid Hollywood Rise

&#x201C;I&#x2019;m not going to lie to you &#x2014; I was in denial,&#x201D; she says with a laugh. &#x201C;I had spent so much time building Ainsley&#x2019;s internal world that I couldn&#x2019;t see that she was funny. As an actor, I had to believe in the absurdity of what was written. But by season two, I was having a blast and leaning into the comedy.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

She&#x2019;s been leaning into it, alright. In fact, this week, Randolph, 29, is departing the dusty plains of Texas and embarking on a screwball road trip in Clashing Through the Snow , a new Prime Video holiday romp that&#x2019;s giddily stuffed with just about every time-honored trope you can find in the book of romcom love.

Meet cute? Couldn&#x2019;t be cuter. Randolph and costar Christopher Briney (best known as the beach-house heartthrob Conrad on Prime&#x2019;s The Summer I Turned Pretty ) play rival book editors at an LA-based romance-novel publishing house who hate each other&#x2019;s guts &#x2014; until the plane they&#x2019;re both flying on gets diverted and they find themselves forced to share the last available rental car for a cross-country trek to New York. Zany antics? How about getting framed for meth possession with rock candy. Snappy banter? &#x201C;I&#x2019;d rather be trapped in a porta potty at Burning Man during an earthquake,&#x201D; Briney zings Randolph at the rental car counter. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Of course, these sorts of frothy shenanigans used to be a big screen staple back when films like Pretty Woman , Sleepless in Seattle and When Harry Met Sally ruled the box office. They were also star-minting machines: Julia Roberts, Tom Hanks, and Meg Ryan all broke through in the genre, along with Sandra Bullock, Cameron Diaz, Hugh Grant, Reese Witherspoon and &#x2014; maybe the last of the line &#x2014; some guy named Glen Powell (also known as Randolph&#x2019;s boyfriend; they&#x2019;ve been dating for about a year).

These days romcoms mostly live on streaming, where their star-making powers are less certain. But for Randolph there&#x2019;s still a big opportunity here. She&#x2019;s already proven her sharp comedic chops with her supporting role on Landman &#x2014; and, before that, her formidable dramatic abilities on a previous Sheridan show, holding her own against Harrison Ford and Helen Mirren in the 2022 Yellowstone prequel 1923 . And she&#x2019;s dabbled in ensemble horror flicks too, most recently with a role in Scream 7 . But now, with Clashing Through the Snow, she&#x2019;s stepping into the center of the story, getting her first crack at carrying a major-studio release as one of its main romantic leads.

And this time, she knows it&#x2019;s not Strindberg.

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s so easy for people to equate seriousness with substance,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;But there&#x2019;s just as much value in storytelling that&#x2019;s just like, &#x2018;Watch this, have fun.&#x2019; Sometimes you want to watch something that&#x2019;s purely meant to make you feel good. Life is unpredictable enough &#x2014; sometimes you just want a predictable ending.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Randolph had been modeling for a couple of years &#x2014; shooting for brands like Forever 21, Skechers, and MAC &#x2014; when her agent suggested she give acting a try. She thought the idea was nuts.

&#x201C;It was just foreign to me,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s just not anything I&#x2019;d ever thought about before. It was so outside my comfort zone. Honestly, given my personality, acting was the strangest job for me to have chosen.&#x201D;

For the first 16 years of her life, that personality leaned more towards Tracy Flick than Cher Horowitz. &#x201C;I was a straight-A student, captain of my sports teams, in student government &#x2014; I was that girl,&#x201D; she recalls of growing up in suburban Walnut Creek, about 25 miles northeast of San Francisco. But when she was 16, her father, a marketing executive, moved the family to Huntington Beach, and suddenly Randolph went full Bella Swan. &#x201C;I was a fish out of water,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;I became more self-conscious and shy. I went from a school of 400 students to 3000 overnight. It was overwhelming. I had to kind of figure out my identity.&#x201D;

Luckily, she had some good role models, starting with her sister, Cassie, who in a few years&#x2019; time would become famous in her own right for nearly turning The Bachelor into a track and field event (more on that later), but back then was studying speech pathology at Biola University in nearby La Mirada. &#x201C;Being her younger sister, I always copy everything Cassie does,&#x201D; she says of her sibling (she also has a younger brother, Landon). &#x201C;So, when she went to college to become a speech therapist, I thought that&#x2019;s what I&#x2019;d do too.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

But, of course, Randolph ended up taking her own path. After getting spotted by modeling scouts in Huntington Beach, she signed with the Wilhelmina agency in 2016. Before long, she was living in L.A., spending her days shooting campaigns for sneakers and sun dresses and her off-hours studying for her bachelor&#x2019;s degree in film from Arizona State University&#x2019;s online program. To make extra cash, she also began dabbling in the newly booming business of social media influencing, peddling everything from mattresses to miniskirts on her growing Instagram account (which today boasts 1.4 million followers).

She might have ignored her agent&#x2019;s suggestion to give acting a try, except she began to notice that she was sort of acting, anyway. &#x201C;Most of the time with modeling, you&#x2019;re in a warehouse in downtown LA with cockroaches,&#x201D; she explains. &#x201C;You&#x2019;re wearing 250 pieces a day. You&#x2019;re so uninspired. But I realized that what I liked about modeling was when I got to create characters. Some shoots have their own theme and story, so it felt like I was telling a story with my modeling. Like I was acting.&#x201D;

Close enough, at any rate, that she decided to enroll in classes and start auditioning. She landed the very first role she tried out for: a doomed teenager in a 2017 made-for-TV horror movie called House of the Witch . &#x201C;The casting director said, &#x2018;Okay, imagine you&#x2019;re seeing the scariest thing you&#x2019;ve ever seen and on three I&#x2019;m going to clap and you react,&#x2019;&#x201D; she remembers her scene-stealing tryout. &#x201C;And when he clapped, I ran to the corner of the room and hid from the camera.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid4' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

From that point, she was hooked. &#x201C;Once I got on that set,&#x201D; she says, &#x201C;I was like, this is what I want to do.&#x201D; But it took a little time for casting agents to catch up. Over the next couple of years, she landed a smattering of roles of various sizes &#x2014; in a 2018 low-budget holiday TV movie called A Snow White Christmas ; the 2019 indie comedy 5 Years Apart ; another horror movie, 2021&#x2019;s The Resort &#x2014; but nothing big enough to quit her day job modeling.

Until Taylor Sheridan came into the picture.

Randolph hadn&#x2019;t seen Yellowstone , Sheridan&#x2019;s popular Paramount+ western series, but her father was a huge fan. So, when she heard that a prequel was being cast, she figured what the heck. &#x201C;I thought there&#x2019;s no way in hell I&#x2019;m even being considered for this,&#x201D; she says, &#x201C;but my dad loves the show, so what&#x2019;s another audition.&#x201D;

She landed the role of Elizabeth Strafford, Jack Dutton&#x2019;s beleaguered Boston-bred bride. But before she started shooting 1923 , she first had to attend Taylor Sheridan&#x2019;s cowboy camp. &#x201C;We would ride all day, immerse ourselves in what it would feel to live in that time period,&#x201D; she recalls her two-week baptism-by-saddle at a dude ranch in Montana. &#x201C;It was painful. My butt was bruised and my legs were sore &#x2014; we&#x2019;d take ice baths in the feeding troughs. But you don&#x2019;t fake anything on a Taylor Sheridan set.&#x201D;

Ironically, she never ended up riding a horse on that show &#x2014; &#x201C;I&#x2019;ll never forgive Taylor for that,&#x201D; she half-jokes &#x2014; but she did get to share screen time with Queen Elizabeth and Han Solo. &#x201C;I&#x2019;d be sitting on the set with Helen and Harrison and it was like, &#x2018;Oh my gosh, this is insane,&#x2019;&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;But you have to just be like, &#x2018;This is normal.&#x2019; Because if it wasn&#x2019;t normal, I couldn&#x2019;t do my scenes with them.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid5' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Just before 1923 premiered in December 2022, Randolph got a call from Sheridan. He wanted her back for season two. But he was also working on a new show about a Texas oilman with a high-maintenance ex-wife, a headstrong son and &#x2014; most pertinent &#x2014; an unruly, spectacularly unfiltered teenage daughter. He told her she was perfect for the part, born to play her. But she still needed to audition. He gave her 12 hours to tape 18 pages of dialogue. Randolph dropped everything, turned off her phone, locked herself in a room, and stayed up all night.

Which is how she ended up with two roles in the Sheridan-verse. Before almost losing both.

&#x201C;I had booked Landman and I had another season of 1923 coming up, so I was feeling very lucky, very privileged,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;Then the SAG-AFTRA strike happened. And I was like, &#x2018;Oh my God. Both shows are going to get cancelled.&#x2019;&#x201D;

Not cancelled, just delayed. In 2024, after the strike settled, Randolph flew to Texas to join Thornton (&#x201C;a father figure,&#x201D; she describes him, believe it or not) on the Landman set. Then, right after wrapping, she turned around and jetted to Montana to shoot season two of 1923 . Two very different characters, two tonally very different shows, but together they had Hollywood giving Randolph a double take. And not just Hollywood. For the first time in her career, she started feeling a little bit famous.

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s been sneaking up on me,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;It doesn&#x2019;t feel the way you think it&#x2019;s going to feel. But all any actor really wants is to have a say in their career. You have so little control in this industry. And fame, oddly, feels like it gives you a little bit more control.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid6' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Until, that is, it doesn&#x2019;t. A few years earlier, in 2019, Randolph got an up-close and way too personal preview of the downsides of celebrity when her sister Cassie went on The Bachelor &#x2014; with a little encouragement from Michelle and their friends. &#x201C;We jokingly told her, &#x2018;You&#x2019;re single, you&#x2019;re young, go on the show,&#x2019; not thinking twice about it,&#x201D; she recalls. But when Cassie decided to break the show&#x2019;s rules by declining to participate in the getting-engaged part of the plotline, all hell broke loose. That season&#x2019;s bachelor, Colton Underwood, responded by hopping a fence to get away from the cameras, leaving the producers scrambling to retrieve him. It made for terrific television, and the internet went wild. But being related to the woman in the center of it, who ended up having to file a temporary restraining order against Underwood, was much less entertaining.

&#x201C;It was a crazy time,&#x201D; Randolph says. &#x201C;It was pretty overwhelming to be thrown into a world like that &#x2014; the social media of it all. People online were so beyond cruel. Sometimes I just want to black it out. Bachelor Nation is&#x2026; well, it&#x2019;s a lot.&#x201D;

The experience has understandably made Randolph hyper-protective of her own private life, particularly when it comes to her relationship with you know who. Ask anything about Glen Powell, and all you&#x2019;ll get is a polite smile so impenetrable you&#x2019;ll think the video link has frozen (she&#x2019;s Zooming from Texas, where she&#x2019;s in the middle of shooting Landman &#x2019;s third season). Where did they meet? How do they their spend time together? What&#x2019;s an average Sunday afternoon like for them? blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid7' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;Nobody&#x2019;s ever asked me that before,&#x201D; she says, not answering the questions.

Fortunately, she&#x2019;s much more talkative when it comes to her on-screen romances &#x2014; especially the one Amazon is releasing Nov. 23, just in time to rouse Prime subscribers from their turkey comas over Thanksgiving break.

To prepare for her performance in Clashing Through the Snow , Randolph didn&#x2019;t have to attend any boot camps. She merely needed to watch some old movies. Or, more precisely, rewatch them. &#x201C;I&#x2019;d seen them all before, but I watched every single romcom &#x2014; anything by Nora Ephron, anything with Meg Ryan falling in love in New York City.&#x201D;

Before filming, she also met with her costar to make sure she and Briney clicked. &#x201C;We did a chemistry read,&#x201D; she says, &#x201C;which was really interesting because in this movie we start out hating each other.&#x201D;

Once it was determined the pair could convincingly pretend to be both annoyed and adoring, they met with director Carlson Young to spend a week working with the script, figuring out just how far they could push the jokes. Briney says that Randolph was particularly good at spotting boundaries. &#x201C;We all looked foolish a few times because you have to do that to find the comedy,&#x201D; he says. &#x201C;But she was really smart about sensing when something didn&#x2019;t feel right. She&#x2019;d be like, &#x2018;What if we try this instead?&#x2019;&#x201D;

