The basic ingredients of the genre haven&#x2019;t changed much over the decades &#x2014; the plot points remain as predictable as the happy endings &#x2014; but one thing is definitely different. Today, romcoms have all but disappeared from the big screen. With a few notable exceptions (like Powell&#x2019;s 2023 hit Anyone but You ), they&#x2019;ve migrated almost entirely to streaming. Netflix pumps them out practically weekly ( Champagne Problems , La Dolce Villa , the just-dropped Guarding Stars ) as does Hulu ( Fire Island , Rye Lane ) and Prime (before Clashing , there was The Idea of You , Picture This , Red, White and Royal Blue , Five Blind Dates , the list goes on).

